  "worked_solution": "Since $(2,4)$ lies on ${f}^{-1},$ we have ${f}^{-1}(2)=4.$ \nThe slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ for $x\\in [1,5]$ is $1$, hence, ${f}^{\u2032}(4)=1.$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse function is \n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
